      "side": 1,
      "message": "What does `shape-root` do at `max_shapes`? Extension falls back to dictionary mode, but dictionary mode needs a root, since the dictionary shape is per root. So a new class, prototype or singleton at the cap can\u0027t be given one. If it raises `LimitExceeded`, catchable as ADR 0023\u0027s caps are, it\u0027s worth saying so. Note that it then hits the per-object roots of item 5 (Ruby singletons, `setPrototypeOf`) too, until collectable shapes land.",
      "revId": "bf956b5c4c46618eb022b8040cfb6a10eb0bde8d",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
