      "side": 1,
      "message": "Item 14 says both that the ES runtime \"interns an ES string key as a symbol on the way in\", and that \"keys that arrive as data and stay strings in a dictionary-mode object are not interned\". It needs one exact rule. Symbols aren\u0027t collected yet (#46), so interning computed keys taken from data (`obj[k] \u003d v` over parsed JSON) grows the symbol table with input until ADR 0023\u0027s cap stops the program.\n\nOne rule that works: intern a key that is a literal, or already an interned symbol (a lookup, not a new symbol), and keep any other computed string key as a string. That moves the object to dictionary mode, which its data-shaped keys would cause anyway. Also, strings compared by content in a dictionary table are mutable in Scheme, so the table should copy, or freeze, a string key when it\u0027s inserted.",
      "revId": "bf956b5c4c46618eb022b8040cfb6a10eb0bde8d",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
